  "_about": "The topic map scripts/mesh.py reads. 'assets' names each asset class (keyed by its hub path, or by a bare key when no hub exists) and puts it in a family; practice-area case lists are grouped by family. 'programs' names each practice area. 'notes' says which asset classes (hubs) and practice areas (programs) each research note informs; program_wide notes are listed on every case in their programs, the others only on cases of their asset classes. A hub lists the notes that name it; a practice area lists the notes that name it; a note lists its hubs, its practice areas, the cases of its hubs and its related notes. Everything else (which state, hub and program each case belongs to) comes from the case pages' own links.",
